"From foreign Invasion, from civil War, from displacing of good and upright Magistrates, from exalting bad and corrupt Men into Office;
Good Lord deliver us.
"O Thou the God and Father of All, deliver me and all Mankind, especially all that need or desire my Prayers, from those grievous Evils to which we are exposed, through the Malice of Evil Spirits, Frailty of our Nature, or Violence of wicked Men, from an uncomfortable Life, in Sadness of Spirit, in Infirmity of Body, ill Reports, Want, in Danger, Imprisonment, Captivity;
Good Lord deliver us.
"From Death in Sin, in Shame, in Torture, in Distraction, in Violence, from unprepared, and from eternal Death;
Good Lord deliver us.
To these Deprecations you may add such further Intercessions, as are suitable to the Design of the Day, and as your own Thoughts suggest, or you may use the Devotions in this or any other Books, making such Enlargements, Alterations, and Applications as will best suit your own Heart, and give you the tenderest Sense of what your own and others Sins deserve, the great Want of Mercy and Pardon; and how intirely you and all Creatures depend on God, for all the Supports and Comforts of Life, and for Preservation from those L.2 Evils

